                                    <watches>3</watches>
                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="17928338" author="JIRAUSER298470" created="Wed, 19 Feb 2025 08:27:09 +0000"  >&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;RootCause&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Root Cause&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The issue is not due to metadata saving failure but rather the incorrect recommendation of `ReusedModels`. In the `modelSuggestionResponse`, there are two models with the same UUID. When updating `reusedModels&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;1&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;`, it overwrites `reusedModels&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;0&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;`. However, `reusedModels&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;0&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;` contains the recommended indexes and computed columns (CC), which are lost in the process. &#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17930084" author="githubbot" created="Tue, 25 Feb 2025 07:02:21 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;gleonSun opened a new pull request, #2291:&lt;br/&gt;
URL: &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/kylin/pull/2291&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/kylin/pull/2291&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;   (no comment)&lt;/p&gt;

</comment>
